## Finding derived from the rerun
The direct probe above evaluates the same seeded baseline that DECISION.md calls an already-released 0.1.0. Under the recommended two flags, a breaking feat!: from 0.1.0 produces 0.2.0, not 0.1.1. Therefore the source establishes only that the seed is treated as the previous released/current version and that the next version depends on subsequent conventional commits; it does not establish an unconditional first Release PR or released version of 0.1.1.
